{
  "_comment": "Counts (owner, 2026-10-22): a count attached to a file word (\"2 of the videos\", \"three of the videos\", \"both mov files\", \"all 3 files\", \"2 от клиповете\", \"两个视频\"; digits and number words in the corpora's languages, the plural file words of many-files batches, at most two words between) must equal the number of files the plan touches, else the run asks. The files touched are the plan's folder and glob inputs after widening, listed like the per-file batch (the skill's file_kinds, natural order), plus any file named beside them; an earlier step's output is not counted again. Only a plan with a folder or a glob is checked: files named one by one are the request's own choice. A number on anything else never counts (seconds, parts, fps, a speed factor). More files than asked: \"Which N of the M <noun>? Name them.\"; fewer: \"I found M <noun> here, not N. Which ones do you mean?\". The noun follows the files' kind (videos, audio files, documents, images, text files), else files. A position word (\"the 3 biggest\") is a count like any other. Python `knaif.nl_clarify_gate.count_question`, Rust `knaif_core::nl_clarify_gate::count_question`.",
  "file_kinds": {
    "mp4": "video",
    "mov": "video",
    "mkv": "video",
    "mp3": "audio",
    "pdf": "document",
    "jpg": "image",
    "txt": "text"
  },
